{"type":"message","id":"0f7ef454","parentId":"93072e81","timestamp":"2026-05-18T03:18:15.917Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The service is up (returns 401 for unauthenticated requests), but 1101 error code from the POST /send endpoint. The 1101 error is a Cloudflare Workers error. Let me try using the `Authorization: Bearer` header instead.\n\nActually wait - the earlier GET requests worked with `X-API-Key` header. So maybe the /send endpoint has an issue, or the payload format.\n\nLet me try with different encoding or a GET request to /send to see if it accepts GET.\n\nActually, let me try to look at what error 1101 actually means. In Cloudflare Workers, error 1101 is \"Worker thrown an exception\" - so the Worker itself is crashing.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-454acf31-8146-42f7-bad7-ec3cbce7f08a","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration&content=Heartbeat+test\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":20348,"output":199,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20659,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779074288776,"responseId":"chatcmpl-d1171291-b454-4e5f-bc4e-b9e819703ea8"}}
